o command is recorded to /var/log/sudo-commands.log with user and timestamp, and no longer reaches the general system log. Previously sudo used its compiled-in default of logging via syslog's authpriv facility straight into /var/log/messages. Added /etc/sudoers.d/sudo-logging with `Defaults !syslog`, `Defaults logfile=\\\"/var/log/sudo-commands.log\\\"`, `Defaults log_year`, `Defaults log_host`, validated with visudo -c, and pre-created the log file (root:root, 600). Verified sudo commands now write entries like `Sep  4 23:08:02 2026 : root : HOST=node1 ; PWD=/ ; USER=root ; COMMAND=...` to the dedicated file while /var/log/messages received no further sudo entries. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id baseline, issued a background `reboot` so the ack returned before disconnect, confirmed the node dropped and came back, proved boot_id changed (cbb5f7ee... -> 45013fd5..., uptime ~16s), and confirmed post-restart that the sudoers drop-in persisted, previously logged entries were retained, new sudo commands continued logging correctly to the dedicated file, and none leaked to /var/log/messages.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/sudo version and current sudo logging behavior (syslog authpriv -> /var/log/messages)\",\"Created /etc/sudoers.d/sudo-logging with Defaults !syslog, logfile, log_year, log_host\",\"Validated sudoers syntax with visudo -c\",\"Pre-created /var/log/sudo-commands.log with root:root 600 permissions\",\"Ran sudo commands and confirmed they logged to the dedicated file with user+timestamp and not to /var/log/messages\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime baseline on node1\",\"Issued backgrounded reboot so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset, proving a real restart\",\"Post-restart: re-validated sudoers config, confirmed prior log entries persisted, confirmed new sudo commands still route only to the dedicated log file\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Sudo commands recorded to /var/log/sudo-commands.log with user and timestamp\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a8ad4cfd7e1f499b\",\"cmd-10d173cbce73430a\"],\"summary\":\"Created and validated sudoers drop-in; log file shows entries like 'Sep 4 23:07:15 2026 : root : HOST=node1 ; PWD=/ ; USER=root ; COMMAND=...'\"},{\"requirement\":\"Entries kept out of the general system log\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-773ad4989e72475b\",\"cmd-10d173cbce73430a\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline showed sudo previously wrote to /var/log/messages via syslog; after the change, /var/log/messages line count stayed flat while new sudo activity only appeared in sudo-commands.log\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5dee1f287d0f43b5\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id cbb5f7ee-4877-4f2a-b797-79af01dff32e, uptime ~82s, sudoers drop-in content, log file permissions, and line counts before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e900ecfba8054bf3\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded reboot command returned REBOOT_ACK_SENT before the node dropped\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b15d63435c3f4372\",\"cmd-85ec39ccdac34646\"],\"summary\":\"Exec failed with connection reset while node was down, then succeeded with new boot_id 45013fd5-e70e-4998-bfbf-014b540ad586 and uptime 15.99s, proving a genuine reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of sudo logging config and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-33023aab72904c73\"],\"summary\":\"Sudoers drop-in intact and valid, prior 14 log lines preserved growing to 18 with new correctly formatted entries, and no corresponding entries appeared in /var/log/messages\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (Alpine 3.23, sudo 1.9.17p2) so every sudo command is recorded to /var/log/sudo-commands.log with user and timestamp, and no longer reaches the general system log. Previously sudo used its compiled-in default of logging via syslog's authpriv facility straight into /var/log/messages. Added /etc/sudoers.d/sudo-logging with `Defaults !syslog`, `Defaults logfile=\"/var/log/sudo-commands.log\"`, `Defaults log_year`, `Defaults log_host`, validated with visudo -c, and pre-created the log file (root:root, 600). Verified sudo commands now write entries like `Sep  4 23:08:02 2026 : root : HOST=node1 ; PWD=/ ; USER=root ; COMMAND=...` to the dedicated file while /var/log/messages received no further sudo entries. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id baseline, issued a background `reboot` so the ack returned before disconnect, confirmed the node dropped and came back, proved boot_id changed (cbb5f7ee... -> 45013fd5..., uptime ~16s), and confirmed post-restart that the sudoers drop-in persisted, previously logged entries were retained, new sudo commands continued logging correctly to the dedicated file, and none leaked to /var/log/messages.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/sudo version and current sudo logging behavior (syslog authpriv -> /var/log/messages)","Created /etc/sudoers.d/sudo-logging with Defaults !syslog, logfile, log_year, log_host","Validated sudoers syntax with visudo -c","Pre-created /var/log/sudo-commands.log with root:root 600 permissions","Ran sudo commands and confirmed they logged to the dedicated file with user+timestamp and not to /var/log/messages","Captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime baseline on node1","Issued backgrounded reboot so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again","Confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset, proving a real restart","Post-restart: re-validated sudoers config, confirmed prior log entries persisted, confirmed new sudo commands still route only to the dedicated log file"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Sudo commands recorded to /var/log/sudo-commands.log with user and timestamp","command_ids":["cmd-a8ad4cfd7e1f499b","cmd-10d173cbce73430a"],"summary":"Created and validated sudoers drop-in; log file shows entries like 'Sep 4 23:07:15 2026 : root : HOST=node1 ; PWD=/ ; USER=root ; COMMAND=...'"},{"requirement":"Entries kept out of the general system log","command_ids":["cmd-773ad4989e72475b","cmd-10d173cbce73430a"],"summary":"Baseline showed sudo previously wrote to /var/log/messages via syslog; after the change, /var/log/messages line count stayed flat while new sudo activity only appeared in sudo-commands.log"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1","command_ids":["cmd-5dee1f287d0f43b5"],"summary":"Captured boot_id cbb5f7ee-4877-4f2a-b797-79af01dff32e, uptime ~82s, sudoers drop-in content, log file permissions, and line counts before restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-e900ecfba8054bf3"],"summary":"Backgrounded reboot command returned REBOOT_ACK_SENT before the node dropped"},{"requirement":"Node restart proven via changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-b15d63435c3f4372","cmd-85ec39ccdac34646"],"summary":"Exec failed with connection reset while node was down, then succeeded with new boot_id 45013fd5-e70e-4998-bfbf-014b540ad586 and uptime 15.99s, proving a genuine reboot"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of sudo logging config and data","command_ids":["cmd-33023aab72904c73"],"summary":"Sudoers drop-in intact and valid, prior 14 log lines preserved growing to 18 with new correctly formatted entries, and no corresponding entries appeared in /var/log/messages"}]},"ttft_ms":11336,"type":"result","duration_ms":114152,"uuid":"5340292e-e6e4-47b1-8954-5ad90e531348","ttft_stream_ms":1293,"time_to_request_ms":82,"first_content_frame_ms":1865,"queued_turn_count":0}
